cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MCP Governance Validation: Six Properties for Evaluating the Security
  Controls Around Agent Tool Ecosystems
message: >-
  If you reference this framework or run one of its experiments, please cite it
  and — more usefully — report the result.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Bindiya
    family-names: Priyadarshini
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7559-3896'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/bin-ini/mcp-governance-validation'
abstract: >-
  Security research has produced extensive benchmarks for the failures of
  systems — vulnerability corpora, exploit suites, attack taxonomies, red-team
  harnesses — but comparatively little work evaluating the governance planes
  enterprises deploy to manage agent ecosystems. This work proposes six
  properties against which such a governance plane can be tested
  (discoverability, integrity, authorization, observability, action
  traceability, containment), each with a measurable and a defined failure
  condition, arranged as a partial order in which discoverability and integrity
  gate the rest. It describes three structural patterns a governance architecture can
  exhibit and specifies four pre-registerable experiments designed to falsify
  the resulting claims. It is a framework paper rather than a results paper: the experiments
  are proposed, not executed.
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agent security
  - agent governance
  - security control evaluation
  - falsifiability
  - prompt injection
  - enterprise security architecture
license: CC-BY-4.0
